      <memberdef kind="variable" id="iproto_8h_1a14511a7b558fd4154aa8ce8b5f4e035e" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>unsigned</type>
        <definition>unsigned iproto_readahead</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>iproto_readahead</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Network readahead. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A signed integer to avoid automatic type coercion to an unsigned type. We assign it without locks in txn thread and use in iproto thread <ndash/> it&apos;s OK that readahead has a stale value while until the thread caches have synchronized, after all, it&apos;s used in new connections only.</para><para>Notice that the default is not a strict power of two. slab metadata takes some space, and we want allocation steps to be correlated to slab buddy sizes, so when we ask slab cache for 16320 bytes, we get a slab of size 16384, not 32768. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
